





cache the per-candidate symbolic Jacobian build (CPU win; memory side shipped)
    -- 2026-05-19 status: MEMORY side shipped via commit e85a9f4
       (`solve_with_robust.jl:38` defaults to `:forwarddiff` instead of
       `:symbolic`). Wallaby's per-iter ~1 MB RSS growth was driven by
       `Symbolics.jacobian + 2× build_function` in `solve_with_robust:98-103`,
       not the structural SI template rebuild — that one is already
       cached once per cell at `optimized_multishot_estimation.jl:1327`.
       MWE in `repro/memory_audit_2026_05_19/symbolics_jac_mwe.jl`
       shows 370× reduction in per-iter RSS slope post-fix. The original
       "intern table holds strong refs" diagnosis was wrong; the leak is
       in the LLVM JIT code cache from `build_function(expression=Val(false))`.
       Full diagnosis at `repro/memory_audit_2026_05_19/FINDINGS.md`.

    -- What still remains (CPU side):
       Even with `:forwarddiff` defaults, every `solve_with_robust` call
       pays the symbolic-build + native-compile cost for the *residual*
       once (line 60-66) — same as the other `homotopy_continuation.jl`
       solvers (audit: 1× build_function per call there too, not a leak).
       For long-multipoint cells (78 candidates on bioh, 220 on crauste)
       that's still N× the cost of a one-shot build.

    -- Proposed refactor (deferred, real ROI):
         * Build symbolic residual + Jacobian of the *template*
           (variables-only; data as parameters) once per cell, right
           after `prepare_si_template_with_structural_fix` returns at
           `optimized_multishot_estimation.jl:1326`.
         * Compile to a `(varlist, data_values)` closure via
           `Symbolics.build_function(expr, vars, data; expression=Val(false))`.
         * For each candidate: `solve_with_robust` gets the cached
           compiled functions instead of re-building. Plumb via an
           optional `cached_funcs::NamedTuple` kwarg.
         * Cache key: (sorted varlist, sorted equation hashes). Rank
           trimming changes the active equation set on some cells —
           fall back to fresh build if the key misses.

    -- Expected impact (CPU only):
         * Wall time on long-multipoint cells: per the original TODO
           estimate, 5-10× faster (e.g. crauste_3_1em8 might drop from
           17 hr → 2-3 hr). The estimate predates Phase 1; with `:forwarddiff`
           the per-candidate cost is just `build_function(residual)` —
           still substantial but smaller than the old 3× build_function.
           Realistic post-Phase-1 estimate: 2-4× wall on long cells.
         * Memory: already fixed; expect no further reduction.
         * Polish: marginal — polish loop terminates faster anyway.

    -- Risks / caveats:
         * Cache invalidation across rank-trimming variants. crauste +
           biohydrogenation + daisy_mamil4 at all 5 noise levels is the
           minimum acceptance gate.
         * If a future benchmark shows wall regressions on small cells
           (cache lookup overhead > rebuild cost on small systems),
           gate the cache on system size.

    -- Files involved:
         * src/core/solve_with_robust.jl (signature: accept cached funcs)
         * src/core/optimized_multishot_estimation.jl (build + plumb cache;
           the existing `reusable_system_cache` at line 1276 is for
           evaluated systems, separate concern)
         * src/core/parameter_estimation.jl (resolve loops)

    -- Out of scope for the immediate next step:
         * `Symbolics.substitute` per-candidate in
           `si_template_integration.jl:207` is a smaller per-call
           contributor (verified via MWE delta in `mwe_run.txt`).
           Defer.

